1
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:05,580
So how does this game work?

2
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:07,190
I just throw out like a real ball?

3
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:09,310
Yep. Just nice and easy, right over the plate.

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,650
All right.

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,070
You suck, Wolowitz!

6
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:15,580
What's that about?

7
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:16,540
I'm heckling you.

8
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,550
It's a beloved part of baseball.

9
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:20,180
He's right.

10
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:21,650
And given that you're probably still waiting

11
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,540
to be picked for a game that was played in fifth grade,

12
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,370
I'm sure you do suck.

13
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:28,520
Hi. What's going on?

14
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,580
Baseball.

15
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:32,810
Okay, this is not what I meant when I said go outside and play.

16
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,510
He's practicing.

17
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:35,590
For what?

18
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:39,350
The Angels wanted an astronaut to throw out the first pitch,

19
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:41,150
so guess who they called?

20
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:42,930
What, you? Really?!

21
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:45,690
Well, a lot of people who weren't available, but then me!

22
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,460
That's so cool! Congratulations.

23
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,680
I guess that makes you the athlete of the group.

24
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,190
Well, not just him!

25
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:55,430
May I remind you that you're talking to the

26
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,180
seeker, beater, chaser and water boy

27
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,990
of the third place Griffith Park Quidditch team.

28
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:02,260
I know.

29
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:03,950
Watching your boyfriend run around with a broomstick

30
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:06,570
between his legs isn't something you forget.

31
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:09,040
C'mon now, throw one.

32
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,630
All right, here we go.

33
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:13,140
You look like a jackass!

34
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:15,830
Cut it out! You're hurting my feelings!

35
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:18,020
Now you know why we're not outside.

36
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:46,480
Did you enjoy my lecture?

37
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,890
No, and neither did our waiter.

38
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,900
Well, if you're going to serve Cornish game hen,

39
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:55,480
you should either be familiar with the history of Cornwall

40
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,330
or be prepared to learn it.

41
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,630
It's hard to argue with that.

42
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:00,520
And I know

43
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,450
because I saw a sad man with a pepper mill

44
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:04,770
desperately try and fail.

45
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:10,830
Hey, how was dinner?

46
00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:13,200
Good, I had Cornish game hen.

47
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,430
Oh, that poor waiter.

48
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:19,700
Sheldon, how about tomorrow night we see a movie?

49
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,590
You guys are going out two nights in a row?

50
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:25,280
I missed a number of date nights while I was on my train trip,

51
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,370
and I'm contractually obligated to make them up

52
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:30,140
under the terms of the Relationship Agreement.

53
00:02:30,730 --> 00:02:32,330
That's so hot.

54
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:36,240
It's better than hot, it's binding.

55
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:39,750
If you're free tomorrow night,

56
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:42,540
I'd love to have you join us on a double date.

57
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:47,770
You are aware that a double date doesn't count as two dates.

58
00:02:51,050 --> 00:02:53,220
Well, then come or don't. I don't care.

59
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,530
I can't believe you're sore.

60
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,660
Hey, even professional pitchers need a rubdown after the game.

61
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:06,680
But they throw an actual ball.

62
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:09,230
You were throwing air at a TV.

63
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:11,870
For your information,

64
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,670
I also gave Leonard one hell of a high five.

65
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,410
I'm kind of surprised you agreed to do this

66
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:19,330
in front of a stadium full of people.

67
00:03:19,330 --> 00:03:21,900
They're doing Space Day and NASA asked me.

68
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,680
I felt like I couldn't say no.

69
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,840
Okay.

70
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,620
Well, if you want, I could help you practice.

71
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:28,520
I played a lot of softball growing up.

72
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,480
Thank you, that would be great.

73
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,510
Great. And while we're at it,

74
00:03:31,510 --> 00:03:32,500
maybe we could butch up your run

75
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,600
for when you head out to the mound.

76
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:37,990
What's wrong with the way I run?

77
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:39,170
Oh, just kidding.

78
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:40,530
Nothing.

79
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:51,780
Sheldon, I'm surprised you'd choose to go to a pub.

80
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,380
At our committee meeting,

81
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:55,940
Amy made a motion for a picnic in a park,

82
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,160
but I tacked so many amendments on that thing

83
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:00,900
it sank like a lead balloon.

84
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:02,670
I then suggested a pub.

85
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:04,870
Yeah, which I was initially skeptical of

86
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:08,280
until I saw online that they serve Yorkshire pudding.

87
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,180
You don't even like Yorkshire pudding.

88
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:11,280
No, it's yucky,

89
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:14,070
but informing people about the history of Yorkshire

90
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:15,930
is yummy, yum-yum.

91
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,620
After a lively debate,

92
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:21,570
that proposal passed by a two-zero margin.

93
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,120
Nice to see a busy couple

94
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,450
keep the spark of bureaucracy alive.

95
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,450
Ignore them, Amy. They're just jealous

96
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:33,760
because they'll never have a relationship as good as ours.

97
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:38,090
Isn't this when he says "bazooka" or something?

98
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,520
I wasn't making a joke,

99
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,360
I was merely stating fact.

100
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:46,360
Amy and I have a superior relationship to yours.

101
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:48,580
You don't honestly think that, do you?

102
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,110
Y... Leonard,

103
00:04:50,110 --> 00:04:52,450
I assumed you knew.

104
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:55,410
The ranking of relationships in our circle

105
00:04:55,410 --> 00:04:57,790
by quality is: me and Amy,

106
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:00,610
Howard and Bernadette, Raj and his girlfriend,

107
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:03,800
Penny and Chardonnay, Penny and you.

108
00:05:06,170 --> 00:05:07,980
There isn't any ranking.

109
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,850
And if there were, we wouldn't be at the bottom of it.

110
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:14,000
Yeah, and actually, I drink Sauvignon Blanc.

111
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:17,790
That's the part you have a problem with?

112
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,600
Relax.

113
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,660
There they go, fighting again.

114
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:25,560
You'd never hear her talk that way to Sauvignon Blanc.

115
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:30,970
So you never played baseball as a kid,

116
00:05:30,970 --> 00:05:32,850
not even Little League?

117
00:05:32,850 --> 00:05:34,880
Well, I was going to, but the day of tryouts

118
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,360
I found my dad's Playboy collection.

119
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:40,970
Threw my arm out.

120
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:45,340
All right, the pitcher's mound in Major League Baseball

121
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:47,720
is 60 feet, six inches away from home plate.

122
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,830
Great. You take this

123
00:05:49,830 --> 00:05:52,170
and say when to stop.

124
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,230
How much further?

125
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:00,620
Keep going.

126
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:04,270
How about now?

127
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:06,140
I'll let you know.

128
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:09,970
Are you saying "stop"

129
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:12,340
and we're just too far away to hear you?

130
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:14,760
Okay, stop.

131
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:20,520
Are you kidding me?!

132
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,120
That's 60 feet.

133
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,530
There's no way this is 60 feet.

134
00:06:24,530 --> 00:06:26,440
I'm looking at it.

135
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,570
You realize this isn't one of those times

136
00:06:29,570 --> 00:06:33,080
I want you to exaggerate how long something is.

137
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:40,050
Okay, I got to... I-I just...

138
00:06:40,050 --> 00:06:41,460
I got to ask:

139
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:44,260
what makes you think that your relationship

140
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:46,890
is so wonderful and ours isn't?

141
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:48,400
For starters,

142
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,110
we enjoy spending time together.

143
00:06:54,450 --> 00:06:55,940
So do we.

144
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:58,180
And I've seen you guys ignore each other for hours

145
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:00,040
doing totally different things.

146
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:03,850
It's called parallel play.

147
00:07:03,850 --> 00:07:05,610
Yeah, toddlers do that.

148
00:07:05,610 --> 00:07:07,160
Not as well as we do.

149
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,060
You believe this guy? He has to be the best at everything.

150
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:14,270
So what? Why do you even care?

151
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,840
Oh, listen to them.

152
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:18,710
Not even married and the honeymoon's over.

153
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,450
Whatever. You can't even go on a date

154
00:07:21,450 --> 00:07:24,010
without checking your relationship agreement.

155
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:27,530
If you've got a problem basing a relationship on a contract,

156
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,830
I'd like to tell you about 13 plucky colonies

157
00:07:30,830 --> 00:07:32,840
that entered a "Relationship agreement"

158
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,430
called the U.S. Constitution.

159
00:07:35,770 --> 00:07:37,690
And it may not be cool to say so,

160
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:40,840
but I think that love affair is still pretty hot today.

161
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,350
It's a good thing I'm not wearing flag underwear right now,

162
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:48,360
 'cause there's about to be a fire.

163
00:07:54,610 --> 00:07:56,050
Okay, it's not that hard.

164
00:07:56,050 --> 00:07:57,850
You just look to where you want to throw it,

165
00:07:57,850 --> 00:07:59,470
step towards where you want to throw,

166
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:00,610
and throw it.

167
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,120
That's your help?

168
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:08,050
That's like saying, "Here's how you fly a plane:

169
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,240
Get in the airplane,

170
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:12,490
know where you want to go and fly it."

171
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:16,780
Just throw the ball. Let's see what we're working with.

172
00:08:26,850 --> 00:08:29,020
Come on Howard, fire it in.

173
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,240
Throw the damn ball!

174
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:04,150
So when do you guys plan on getting married?

175
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,280
Uh, we're not sure. But I want to wait long enough

176
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,810
to prove to my mother I'm not pregnant.

177
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,190
May I have one of your fries?

178
00:09:12,190 --> 00:09:13,320
Of course.

179
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:15,740
Can I have a bite of your burger?

180
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,420
Absolutely not.

181
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:20,220
Some perfect couple.

182
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:21,900
He won't even share his food with her.

183
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,850
It has avocado on it.

184
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:25,890
She's allergic to avocado.

185
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:28,040
Are you so jealous of our relationship

186
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,090
you want Amy to die?

187
00:09:32,130 --> 00:09:33,120
I'm not jealous.

188
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,580
I just think it's silly for you to compare relationships

189
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:38,010
like they're something that can be quantified.

190
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:39,990
Everything is quantifiable.

191
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:42,380
That French fry? A seven.

192
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:44,650
Spider-Man? A nine.

193
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:48,040
The number nine-- oddly, only a four.

194
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,410
- How ridiculous is he? - A hundred.

195
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:56,750
Sheldon, you're just assigning random numbers

196
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,520
to things based on your opinion.

197
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,800
No, I'm not.

198
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,820
French fries have three variables--

199
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:03,960
crispiness, saltiness and shape.

200
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:06,550
Which is why a curly fry only gets a two.

201
00:10:06,790 --> 00:10:10,100
If I wanted curls for dinner, I'd order a clown wig.

202
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:14,930
Well, a relationship is more complicated than a French fry.

203
00:10:14,930 --> 00:10:18,460
Not according to the work of Berscheid, Snyder and Omoto.

204
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:21,050
Oh, what did those rascals do now?

205
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:25,040
They developed the Relationship Closeness Inventory,

206
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:27,750
which predicts the stability of a couple based on behavior.

207
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:29,190
Yeah, not to be confused

208
00:10:29,190 --> 00:10:31,190
with the French Fry Goodness Inventory.

209
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:33,010
That's pure Cooper.

210
00:10:34,270 --> 00:10:35,560
So, this is accurate?

211
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,360
It's been around for 25 years,

212
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:40,190
and has been extensively corroborated by other researchers.

213
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:42,740
Well, kind of takes the romance out of relationships.

214
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,940
Kind of? It does it perfectly.

215
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,060
Sheldon and I got an eight-point-two out of ten.

216
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:51,480
Fine. We'll take it right now.

217
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,510
- No, don't. - What?

218
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:55,030
- Just don't take it. - Why not?

219
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:56,770
'Cause it's stupid. Who cares what number it is?

220
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:57,920
Come on. It'll be fun.

221
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,840
I said I don't want you to.

222
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:02,580
I'm getting another drink.

223
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:05,720
Sorry.

224
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:10,920
I'm gonna let you count this as two dates.

225
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,680
They're a lot of work.

226
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,200
Think he's getting any better?

227
00:11:23,730 --> 00:11:24,600
Yup.

228
00:11:25,970 --> 00:11:27,630
That was a close one!

229
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:28,960
Okay!

230
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,260
Is it too late for him to cancel?

231
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:33,850
I think so.

232
00:11:38,930 --> 00:11:41,030
Heads up! Watch out!

233
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:50,180
Are you mad at me?

234
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:52,510
No, stop being stupid.

235
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:55,130
Um... whew?

236
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:00,080
Is this about the test, or is this about us?

237
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,200
Look, I don't need a score on a test

238
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,470
to make me worry about something I'm already worried about.

239
00:12:03,470 --> 00:12:04,900
What are you worried about?

240
00:12:05,690 --> 00:12:08,100
That we're engaged and have nothing in common,

241
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:10,020
and it scares me.

242
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:13,370
Yeah, that scares me, too.

243
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:14,480
It does?

244
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,990
Sometimes.

245
00:12:15,990 --> 00:12:18,100
Well, that's not good!

246
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:22,200
You being blindly infatuated with me was the rock

247
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,460
we were building this relationship on!

248
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:28,820
Okay, well, this might make you feel better.

249
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:32,960
Uh, we're both scared that our marriage will be a disaster,

250
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,700
and so, that's something that we have in common.

251
00:12:41,150 --> 00:12:44,410
Also, we both think I'm not funny.

252
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:47,880
Huh? See, you're not laughing.

253
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,780
Hey, Froot Loops, what's up?

254
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:56,760
Hey, Mike.

255
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:59,170
Listen, NASA asked me to

256
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:02,370
throw out the first pitch at an Angels game.

257
00:13:02,370 --> 00:13:03,910
You got any advice?

258
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:06,080
Yeah. Don't do it.

259
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,400
What else you up to?

260
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,310
Why shouldn't I do it?

261
00:13:11,310 --> 00:13:12,530
There's no upside.

262
00:13:12,530 --> 00:13:15,230
If you do well, no one cares.

263
00:13:15,230 --> 00:13:16,510
And if you screw up,

264
00:13:16,510 --> 00:13:18,830
you're an idiot on YouTube forever.

265
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:22,860
But it's for a good cause.

266
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,680
What about all the kids that'll be there?

267
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,100
That's what I'm telling you.

268
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,930
Kids are the worst.

269
00:13:29,410 --> 00:13:32,620
My own daughter tweeted I have a giant nose.

270
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:36,830
Well, maybe I'll do a good job.

271
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:37,920
I don't know.

272
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,880
In space, you couldn't even toss me a pen,

273
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,860
and that was in zero gravity.

274
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,840
Okay, thanks for the pep talk.

275
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,670
Anytime, Froot Loops.

276
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,770
Give your wife a hug for me.

277
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:50,970
She's so much cuter than you,

278
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:52,770
I don't know how you ever got her.

279
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,890
He's so nice.

280
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,490
Hey, sorry about that.

281
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:04,970
No, we're sorry.

282
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:08,150
We never should have been comparing relationships in the first place.

283
00:14:08,150 --> 00:14:10,420
Why? We won.

284
00:14:11,590 --> 00:14:14,420
You know, I say, next, we take on Koothrappali and his dog.

285
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:16,480
Really give ourselves a challenge.

286
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:18,970
I just want to say one more thing about this.

287
00:14:18,970 --> 00:14:21,250
Just because Penny and I are very different people

288
00:14:21,250 --> 00:14:23,640
does not mean that we're a bad couple.

289
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,740
The answer is one simple test away.

290
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,220
You know, it's like when I thought

291
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:30,360
there was a possum in my closet.

292
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,960
Did I sit around wondering?

293
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:35,850
No, I sent Leonard in with a pointy stick and a bag.

294
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:39,040
I killed his Chewbacca slippers.

295
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:43,430
Let's just take the test.

296
00:14:43,430 --> 00:14:44,700
No, no, no, I don't want to.

297
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:46,360
Oh, well, 'cause you know we're gonna do bad.

298
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,710
Because it doesn't matter.

299
00:14:47,710 --> 00:14:50,190
I don't care if we're a ten or a two.

300
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:52,980
Or a one. A one is possible.

301
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:56,310
Marriage is scary.

302
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:57,860
You're scared, I'm scared.

303
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:00,690
But it doesn't make me not want to do it.

304
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:01,690
It-it just...

305
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:05,950
makes me want to hold your hand and do it with you.

306
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,260
Leonard...

307
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:14,910
It would make me so happy if you said things like that.

308
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:16,360
We got an eight-point-two.

309
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:18,030
Trust me, you're happy.

310
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,880
I love how they put a waterfall at center field.

311
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:33,850
It really ties the whole stadium together.

312
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:36,040
Look at you, talking sports.

313
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,440
This is fun, huh?

314
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:41,350
We get to see our friend throw out the first pitch,

315
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:43,040
have a hot dog, watch the game.

316
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:47,640
Nobody said anything about watching the game.

317
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,060
Sheldon, what did you expect?

318
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:53,650
I expected to see Howard throw the baseball,

319
00:15:53,650 --> 00:15:55,140
finish my hot dog,

320
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:57,080
and hightail it across the street to Disneyland

321
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,850
just in time for Mickey's Soundsational Parade.

322
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:02,290
I'll tell you what.

323
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:05,550
If we stay, I'll buy you cotton candy and a bobblehead.

324
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:08,610
Who's the bobblehead of?

325
00:16:08,610 --> 00:16:10,250
Does it matter?

326
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:12,760
No, as long as it bobbles.

327
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:17,210
Howie, I am so proud of you.

328
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:19,520
Thanks. I'm proud of me, too.

329
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:21,630
You ready?

330
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:23,140
Let's do it.

331
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:24,180
All right.

332
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:28,170
Wish me luck.

333
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:29,290
Go get 'em.

334
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:30,610
Ladies and gentlemen,

335
00:16:30,610 --> 00:16:33,160
in honor of Space Day at Angel Stadium,

336
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,780
the first pitch will be thrown out

337
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:37,780
by NASA astronaut Howard Wolowitz.

338
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:42,490
Thank you.

339
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,330
Thank you.

340
00:16:44,950 --> 00:16:46,230
Can he really throw a ball?

341
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:48,800
- On our Quidditch team, he... - Yeah, that's a "No."

342
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:54,840
I have a message for the young people here today.

343
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:58,190
When I was asked to throw the first pitch,

344
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:03,590
a little voice in my head said I couldn't do it.

345
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:06,720
So, I practiced and practiced,

346
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,280
and you know what?

347
00:17:08,650 --> 00:17:10,260
That little voice...

348
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:13,090
...was right, but...

349
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:19,010
...then I remembered that I'm not an athlete.

350
00:17:19,010 --> 00:17:21,240
I'm a scientist.

351
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,460
So, today's first pitch

352
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:27,490
will be delivered to home plate by science.

353
00:17:27,490 --> 00:17:28,790
Ladies and gentlemen,

354
00:17:28,790 --> 00:17:31,090
boys and girls, I present to you

355
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:36,920
a working prototype of the Mars Rover!

356
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:44,070
And here's the wind-up...

357
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,640
and the pitch!

358
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,290
Why is it going so slow?!

359
00:18:00,290 --> 00:18:03,130
'Cause I'm an idiot who didn't think this through!

360
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:05,700
Okay, new plan.

361
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:07,500
We go to Disneyland,

362
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,730
play hide and seek on Tom Sawyer's Island,

363
00:18:09,730 --> 00:18:12,800
and then come back and see the end of the pitch.

364
00:18:22,490 --> 00:18:25,140
Okay, while we're waiting for the ball to arrive,

365
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:27,470
here's some fun facts about Mars.

366
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:29,690
You suck, Wolowitz!

367
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:34,510
He makes a valid point!

368
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:53,280
Okay, booing isn't gonna make it go any faster!

